  "summary": "DPRK-aligned Contagious Interview actors target developers with fake job interviews and trojanized Next.js e-commerce take-home projects whose malicious code is hidden as Base64 fragments inside SVG flag images and reassembled via eval() on server start. The four-stage, OTTERCOOKIE-aligned payload steals browser credentials, crypto-wallet LevelDB stores, developer files and clipboard data, and installs a Socket.IO backdoor with a Windows PE dropper. All C2, upload and download activity is hosted under the rightwidth[.]dev domain family.",
